    "cli.surface.usage": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Usage: cmux surface ls [<machine>|local] [--refresh] [--json]\n       cmux surface open <resource> [--workspace <id|ref|index>] [--pane <id|ref>] [--left|--right|--up|--down|--tab] [--new] [--focus <true|false>]\n       cmux surface new-terminal --machine <id|local> [--cwd <dir>] [--name <name>] [--remote-workspace <ws_…>] [--workspace <id|ref|index>] [--no-open] [-- <command...>]\n       cmux surface resume set [flags] -- <argv...>\n       cmux surface resume set [flags] --shell <command>\n       cmux surface resume show [--json] [flags]\n       cmux surface resume get [--json] [flags]\n       cmux surface resume clear [flags]\n       cmux surface size|participants [--surface <id|ref|index>] [--json]\n       cmux surface size-policy <latest|smallest|largest|priority|fixed> [--cols <n> --rows <n>] [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n       cmux surface size-to-me|disconnect-others [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n       cmux surface size-counts <true|false|auto> [--participant <id>] [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n       cmux surface disconnect-participant <participant-id> [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n\nls / open / new-terminal: the surface catalog. Terminals, VNC screens and browsers\non This Mac and on every cloud machine are resources (`<machine>/<kind>/<key>`,\ne.g. local/terminal/<uuid>, vivid-newt/terminal/term_2f9c…, vivid-newt/display/display:1,\nvivid-newt/browser/port:3000); panes project them. `open` reuses the pane already\nshowing a resource unless --new; --pane with a side splits that pane on that side,\n--tab adds a tab to it. A local terminal moves to the destination (it is shown once).\n`new-terminal` creates a terminal on the machine (cloud: in its cmux-tui session).\n`cmux vm tree` prints the same catalog.\n\nresume: attach restart command metadata to a terminal surface.\nPublic CLI bindings are stored for inspection and manual restore.\n\nFlags:\n  --workspace <id|ref|index>   Workspace context (default: $CMUX_WORKSPACE_ID)\n  --surface <id|ref|index>     Surface context (default: $CMUX_SURFACE_ID)\n  --window <id|ref|index>      Window context for workspace and surface refs/indexes\n  --cwd <path>             Working directory for restore (default: $PWD)\n  --name <name>            Display name for the binding\n  --kind <kind>            Binding kind, for example agent or tmux\n  --checkpoint <id>        Provider checkpoint or session id\n  --checkpoint-id <id>     Same as --checkpoint and takes precedence\n  --source <source>        Binding source label\n\nExamples:\n  cmux surface resume set --kind tmux --shell \"tmux attach -t work\"\n  cmux surface resume set --kind opencode --checkpoint ses_123 -- opencode --session ses_123\n  cmux surface resume show --json"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "用法：cmux surface ls [<machine>|local] [--refresh] [--json]\n       cmux surface open <resource> [--workspace <id|ref|index>] [--pane <id|ref>] [--left|--right|--up|--down|--tab] [--new] [--focus <true|false>]\n       cmux surface new-terminal --machine <id|local> [--cwd <dir>] [--name <name>] [--remote-workspace <ws_…>] [--workspace <id|ref|index>] [--no-open] [-- <command...>]\n       cmux surface resume set [flags] -- <argv...>\n       cmux surface resume set [flags] --shell <command>\n       cmux surface resume show [--json] [flags]\n       cmux surface resume get [--json] [flags]\n       cmux surface resume clear [flags]\n       cmux surface size|participants [--surface <id|ref|index>] [--json]\n       cmux surface size-policy <latest|smallest|largest|priority|fixed> [--cols <n> --rows <n>] [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n       cmux surface size-to-me|disconnect-others [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n       cmux surface size-counts <true|false|auto> [--participant <id>] [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n       cmux surface disconnect-participant <participant-id> [--surface <id|ref|index>]\n\nls / open / new-terminal：表面目录。本机与每台云端机器上的终端、VNC 屏幕和浏览器\n都是资源（`<machine>/<kind>/<key>`，例如 local/terminal/<uuid>、\nvivid-newt/terminal/term_2f9c…、vivid-newt/display/display:1、\nvivid-newt/browser/port:3000）；窗格是它们的投影。除非加 --new，`open` 会复用\n已显示该资源的窗格；--pane 配合方向会把该窗格朝那一侧拆分，--tab 则给它加一个标签页。\n本机终端会移动到目标位置（它同时只显示一处）。\n`new-terminal` 会在该机器上创建终端（云端：在其 cmux-tui 会话中）。\n`cmux vm tree` 打印同一份目录。\n\nresume：为终端表面附加重启命令元数据。\n公开的 CLI 绑定会被存储，供查看和手动恢复。\n\n标志:\n  --workspace <id|ref|index>   工作区上下文（默认：$CMUX_WORKSPACE_ID）\n  --surface <id|ref|index>     表面上下文（默认：$CMUX_SURFACE_ID）\n  --window <id|ref|index>      工作区与表面引用/索引的窗口上下文\n  --cwd <path>             恢复时使用的工作目录（默认：$PWD）\n  --name <name>            该绑定的显示名称\n  --kind <kind>            绑定类型，例如 agent 或 tmux\n  --checkpoint <id>        提供方的检查点或会话 id\n  --checkpoint-id <id>     与 --checkpoint 相同，且优先级更高\n  --source <source>        绑定来源标签\n\n示例:\n  cmux surface resume set --kind tmux --shell \"tmux attach -t work\"\n  cmux surface resume set --kind opencode --checkpoint ses_123 -- opencode --session ses_123\n  cmux surface resume show --json"
          }
        }
      }
    },
